  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nfor 13.2.4 \"Verify that REST services have anti-automation controls to protect against excessive calls, especially if the API is unauthenticated.\" you chose to map this to \"CWE-779: Logging of Excessive Data\" instead of \"CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling\".\r\nAre there any specific reasons why CWE-779 is a better fit or is it just the \"most commony used\" as described in the \"What's new in 4.0\" section?\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\nMatthias",
